Received an Aderant email dated 31 August 2026 titled “Final Reminder: Microsoft's Recommended EWS Extension Deadline Is Today.”

The email advises firms using CompuLaw Vision Sync with Exchange Online that Microsoft is retiring Exchange Web Services (EWS) and that they should either:
complete the required Microsoft Graph upgrade, or
enable Microsoft's temporary EWS extension as an interim measure.

Aderant states that without either the Graph upgrade or temporary EWS extension, firms may experience:
interruption/loss of CompuLaw Vision Sync functionality;
Outlook calendar events/deadlines not synchronizing correctly; and
reduced visibility of CompuLaw deadlines in Outlook.

The email states that the temporary EWS extension is only a temporary measure and is valid until 1 April 2027, when EWS will be permanently retired.

--------------------------------------
CompuLaw is installed in the environment.
Investigation of the RDS server did not identify the Vision Sync installation.
The DC server, however, contains the Vision Sync installation under:
C:\Program Files (x86)\Vision Sync for Exchange\
The Vision Sync configuration file was located and reviewed.
The configuration contains:
<Office365EwsUrl>https://outlook.office365.com/EWS/Exchange.asmx</Office365EwsUrl>
<ForceOffice365EwsUrl>true</ForceOffice365EwsUrl>
This confirms that the currently configured synchronization path is Exchange Online EWS.

The configuration also contains an Azure/Entra Client ID, which corresponds to the CompuLaw Modern Authentication Enterprise Application found in Microsoft Entra ID.
The Enterprise Application has both Microsoft Graph permissions and Exchange Online/EWS permissions.
However, the presence of Microsoft Graph permissions does not mean Vision Sync has already been migrated to Graph.
Aderant's separate verification article states that a successful Graph conversion should show:
<UseEWSNoAnchorMbx>false</UseEWSNoAnchorMbx>
whereas the current configuration found on the server has
<UseEWSNoAnchorMbx>true</UseEWSNoAnchorMbx>

According to Aderant's documentation, true means EWS synchronization, while false means Microsoft Graph synchronization



